course: dictionary
lesson: 4109
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Glace is a good example: you can find it in a cake recipe, on a shop sign and in a French lesson. The words around it tell you which meaning is right.
explain: In food, glacé cherries are sweet cherries cooked in sugar syrup, so they look shiny. Glacé icing is a simple runny icing made from icing sugar and water. Both are English food words, and the words next to glacé show which one you mean.
explain: In French, «glace» means ice or ice cream. «Quel parfum ?» means "Which flavour?", and parfum means both perfume and flavour, so the question tells you it is about flavour. On the kids' menu, «glace à la vanille» is vanilla ice cream.
fact: Glacé (often written glace) describes fruit, such as cherries, cooked in sugar syrup so it is shiny and sweet.
fact: Glacé icing is a simple runny icing made from icing sugar and water.
fact: Glacé leather is very shiny smooth leather.
fact: In French, «une glace» means an ice cream, and it is said "glass".
fact: Common French flavours for «glace» are vanille, chocolat, fraise and citron.
exercise: In a cake recipe it says «glacé cherries». What are glacé cherries? | Cherries dried in the sun for a salad | Sour green cherries eaten raw | *Bright red sweet cherries cooked in sugar syrup | Small cherries used in soup
exercise: Dad says «Une glace, s'il te plaît» at a café in Paris. What does he want? | *An ice cream | A bag of crisps | A glass of water | A cup of hot chocolate
exercise: The server asks «Quel parfum ?». What does it mean? | How much does it cost? | *Which flavour? | What is your name? | Where is the toilet?
test: What is glacé icing made from? | *Icing sugar and water | Milk and eggs | Flour and butter
test: On the menu «glace à la vanille - 9,50 €», what does the comma in 9,50 stand for? | A mistake in the price | A list separator | A full stop at the end of a sentence | *A decimal point, as in 9.50 in English
exam: In «glacé leather», what does glacé mean? | Cold, like ice | *Very shiny and smooth | Made from milk | Cooked in sugar syrup
